          Most buying guides treat "concrete floor coating" as a single product category and just rank brands. That's the wrong frame. Epoxy, polyaspartic, polyurea, and polyurethane are four distinct chemistries with different cure chemistry, different bond mechanisms, and different failure modes. Pick the wrong chemistry for your floor's actual conditions and no amount of brand reputation will save the installation.
